---
description: Currency symbol, text casing, dropdown arrows and sidebar typography for the ERP web UI
globs: apps/web/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

# Currency

- The only currency prefix shown to users is `Rs.` Never render `रू`, `रु`, `₨`, `NPR` or a bare `$` in the UI.
- Format amounts through `formatCurrency` / `CURRENCY_SYMBOL` in `apps/web/lib/currency.ts`. Do not inline a new `Rs.` template string or a new per-page `money()` formatter.
- Column headers and units that need the currency inline write it as `(Rs.)`, for example `Price (Rs.)` and `Sub Total (Rs.)`.
- Server-rendered documents (invoice, quotation and purchase-order HTML in `apps/api`) use the same `Rs.` prefix.
- `currencyCode` on the company record stays an ISO code such as `NPR`; that is data, not a display symbol.

# Text Casing

- User-facing labels use proper case (Title Case): buttons and action links (`Generate Invoice`, `Save Payment`), form field labels (`First Name`, `Tax Number`), dropdown options (`All Statuses`, `Select Vendor`), card and section headings, and tab labels.
- Keep short prepositions, articles and conjunctions lowercase inside a title: `Out of Stock`, `Date of Birth`, `Terms & Conditions`.
- Acronyms stay uppercase: `DO`, `PO`, `CRM`, `SMTP`, `VAT`, `S/N`.
- Helper text, placeholders, empty states, error messages and other full sentences stay sentence case.
- Do not use `uppercase` CSS on button or action-link text.
- Table column headers, small eyebrow labels and sidebar section titles may stay uppercase. Status chips that are not buttons may stay as designed.

# Dropdowns

- Use the shared `Select` from `@/components/ui` for page filters and form dropdowns. Do not use a raw `<select>` for those controls.
- Match the product page chevron: hide the native arrow with `appearance-none` and `pr-10`, then place `ChevronDown` at `absolute right-4 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-slate-700`.
- For a compact select that cannot use `Select` (nested label or tiny control), wrap it in `relative` and use the same chevron placement, scaled only if the control is smaller than the default field.

# Sidebar

- Every navigation row — top level, expandable group and nested child — shares the `navRowClass` typography in `apps/web/components/layout/sidebar.tsx`, so all labels render at the same size as `Dashboard`.
- Row icons are `16` when the sidebar is expanded and `18` when collapsed, in every row variant.
